1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,630
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,630 --> 00:00:05,150
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:06,400
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,450 --> 00:00:08,970
I've been a boilermaker
for thirty years.

5
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:11,540
Climbing, kneeling and
hauling steel

6
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:13,550
inside boilers and tanks,

7
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:14,610
every shift.

8
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:15,800
I had my right knee

9
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:17,290
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:17,410 --> 00:00:19,380
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:19,510 --> 00:00:20,860
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:22,610
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:22,610 --> 00:00:23,680
and it went away.

14
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:24,990
This is different.

15
00:00:25,030 --> 00:00:25,440
Tight.

16
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:26,160
Full.

17
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:27,100
Like a band around

18
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,850
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:29,850
And for two years I've

20
00:00:29,850 --> 00:00:31,230
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:32,160
Give it time.

22
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:34,150
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:35,630
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:35,890 --> 00:00:36,660
At three months,

25
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:37,600
give it six.

26
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:38,480
At six months,

27
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,090
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:40,980
At a year,

29
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:42,850
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:44,120
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:45,520
We went down the list.

32
00:00:45,910 --> 00:00:47,310
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,300
Every session,

34
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:49,760
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:49,910 --> 00:00:51,070
I got stronger.

36
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:52,720
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:52,790 --> 00:00:54,210
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:54,210 --> 00:00:55,580
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:55,690 --> 00:00:57,660
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:58,750
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:58,750 --> 00:00:59,970
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:00,270 --> 00:01:01,400
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:02,870
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:02,910 --> 00:01:04,170
And after that, a second

45
00:01:04,170 --> 00:01:05,870
operation to go back in

46
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:06,910
and do it over.

47
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:07,870
I said no.

48
00:01:07,970 --> 00:01:09,880
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:10,920
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:12,400
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,760
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:16,340
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:17,760
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:18,930
Couldn't climb a ladder

55
00:01:18,930 --> 00:01:20,280
at work without stopping,

56
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:21,620
couldn't do the stairs,

57
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:22,690
couldn't stand at the
counter

58
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:24,870
long enough to finish
dinner,

59
00:01:24,870 --> 00:01:26,370
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

60
00:01:26,370 --> 00:01:28,520
game without shifting
every two minutes.

61
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:30,070
It woke me at night,

62
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:32,270
and it turned ordinary
things,

63
00:01:32,270 --> 00:01:33,590
like getting in the truck

64
00:01:33,590 --> 00:01:35,000
or up off the couch,

65
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,110
into a decision.

66
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:37,790
At work I couldn't kneel

67
00:01:37,790 --> 00:01:39,560
inside a boiler anymore,

68
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:41,090
so the younger guys on my
crew

69
00:01:41,090 --> 00:01:42,060
did it for me.

70
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:43,650
Nobody said anything.

71
00:01:43,730 --> 00:01:44,800
They didn't have to.

72
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:46,230
After a long and serious

73
00:01:46,230 --> 00:01:47,260
talk with my wife,

74
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:49,410
I went back in one more
time.

75
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:50,780
That was the fourth set

76
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:52,300
of X-rays on this knee.

77
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:53,880
And like the three before
it,

78
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:56,310
the answer was everything
looks great.

79
00:01:56,470 --> 00:01:58,620
No loosening, no
infection,

80
00:01:58,620 --> 00:01:59,660
nothing wrong.

81
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:01,120
Only this time

82
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:02,610
there was no new number.

83
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:05,240
Nobody said give it
another six months.

84
00:02:05,310 --> 00:02:07,120
There was nothing left to
give it.

85
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:08,160
I sat in the parking

86
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,070
lot for a while.

87
00:02:09,110 --> 00:02:10,200
Okay, I thought.

88
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:11,770
Then explain this.

89
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:14,190
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

90
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:15,650
I hit my breaking point.

91
00:02:15,990 --> 00:02:18,040
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

92
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,050
Everyone in the house was
asleep

93
00:02:20,050 --> 00:02:21,770
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

94
00:02:21,770 --> 00:02:22,960
with my leg up,

95
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:25,100
trying to find any angle
where

96
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,350
it didn't feel like
something

97
00:02:26,350 --> 00:02:28,630
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

98
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:29,650
I had to be

99
00:02:29,650 --> 00:02:31,200
at the plant at six.

100
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,150
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

101
00:02:34,290 --> 00:02:36,040
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

102
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:37,350
And I just thought,

103
00:02:37,350 --> 00:02:39,240
is this really my life
now?

104
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:40,890
I can't live like this.

105
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:42,950
So I made myself a
promise.

106
00:02:42,990 --> 00:02:44,010
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:44,010 --> 00:02:45,640
without looking for an
answer.

108
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,080
And when I found one,

109
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,160
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:49,480
going through the same
thing.

111
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:50,630
So I got my laptop

112
00:02:50,630 --> 00:02:52,110
out and went looking.

113
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:53,410
Not for a product.

114
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:54,630
For an explanation.

115
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,720
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:58,780
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

117
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:01,370
doctor videos, medical
animations.

118
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:02,920
And that's when I found a
video

119
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:05,200
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

120
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,490
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

121
00:03:07,490 --> 00:03:09,530
had been through exactly
this.

122
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,880
But before I say anything
else,

123
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:13,320
I want to be straight with
you.

124
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:15,880
You've already had
something work fast.

125
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:16,750
The ice.

126
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:18,640
The first week of a new
pill.

127
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,550
The good day after a
session.

128
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:22,200
Then it wore off.

129
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:24,430
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

130
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:26,380
Fast relief isn't relief.

131
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:27,360
It's a preview.

132
00:03:27,890 --> 00:03:28,910
So I'm not going to tell

133
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:30,240
you this works fast.

134
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:31,110
It doesn't.

135
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:33,080
But if you're willing to
be patient,

136
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:34,150
and to look at what's
going

137
00:03:34,150 --> 00:03:35,260
on around your new knee

138
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:36,950
instead of inside it,
there

139
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:38,940
is a real reason it still
hurts.

140
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,830
And something you can do
about it.

141
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:42,970
Let me explain what he
said,

142
00:03:42,970 --> 00:03:44,410
because this is what
changed

143
00:03:44,410 --> 00:03:45,650
everything for me.

144
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:47,660
He started with the
basics.

145
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:49,250
A knee replacement takes
out

146
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:50,880
the worn joint surfaces

147
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:52,840
and puts in metal and
plastic.

148
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:54,790
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

149
00:03:54,790 --> 00:03:56,470
you had before the
operation.

150
00:03:56,610 --> 00:03:57,950
That part I already knew.

151
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,560
But then he explained
something

152
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:00,850
nobody had ever told me.

153
00:04:00,890 --> 00:04:01,270
He said,

154
00:04:01,270 --> 00:04:02,580
think about a swollen foot

155
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:03,640
inside a shoe.

156
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:05,230
The shoe didn't shrink.

157
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:08,090
Your foot is taking up
more room,

158
00:04:08,090 --> 00:04:09,970
so everything feels
cramped

159
00:04:09,970 --> 00:04:11,780
and tight and squeezed.

160
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,350
Your new knee sits

161
00:04:13,350 --> 00:04:14,940
in a limited space with
living

162
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:16,680
tissue packed all around
it.

163
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:19,180
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

164
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:20,920
had to work through that
tissue.

165
00:04:21,130 --> 00:04:24,030
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

166
00:04:24,610 --> 00:04:25,890
At first that's normal.

167
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:27,390
But in some people

168
00:04:27,390 --> 00:04:28,700
that swelling can stay
switched

169
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:30,680
on far longer than
expected.

170
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:32,680
And swollen tissue takes
up more

171
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,490
room than calm tissue
does.

172
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:35,860
So when you bend,

173
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:37,490
that tissue gets
compressed.

174
00:04:37,690 --> 00:04:38,690
When you straighten,

175
00:04:38,690 --> 00:04:39,810
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:40,110 --> 00:04:41,240
That's the band.

177
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,560
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

178
00:04:43,670 --> 00:04:44,490
And you start being

179
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:45,500
the one who says,

180
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:46,430
you go ahead.

181
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:47,520
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:47,790 --> 00:04:49,420
And that's exactly why so
much

183
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:51,040
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

184
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:53,420
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,260
around the knee.

186
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,320
Worth doing,

187
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:56,190
and I'd done it.

188
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,670
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:04:57,670 --> 00:04:58,730
taking up room.

190
00:04:59,030 --> 00:05:00,260
A nerve block quiets

191
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:01,780
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,450
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:06,530
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:05:06,530 --> 00:05:08,260
finally calms down,

195
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:09,880
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:11,390
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:11,590 --> 00:05:12,810
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:14,670
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:14,870 --> 00:05:16,660
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:16,990 --> 00:05:18,480
After two years of this,

201
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,070
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,330
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:22,510 --> 00:05:24,400
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:26,270
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:28,810
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,580
I'd bought knee sleeves,

207
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,180
compression braces,

208
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:34,710
creams, half of Amazon
really,

209
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:35,970
and all any of it gave

210
00:05:35,970 --> 00:05:37,050
me was an hour.

211
00:05:37,350 --> 00:05:38,430
I even looked at going

212
00:05:38,430 --> 00:05:40,340
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

213
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:42,480
But at $200 a session

214
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:44,280
with nothing covered by
insurance,

215
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:45,640
that was a quick no.

216
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,740
Then one night I went

217
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:48,020
back to that knee
replacement

218
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:49,490
group and actually read
it.

219
00:05:49,770 --> 00:05:51,110
Thousands of people,

220
00:05:51,110 --> 00:05:52,740
years out from surgery,

221
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:55,060
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

222
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,400
nobody could explain.

223
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:58,520
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

224
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:00,300
the same thing kept coming
up.

225
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:02,340
This one device,

226
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:03,850
and people saying it was
the first

227
00:06:03,850 --> 00:06:05,220
thing that made a
difference.

228
00:06:05,470 --> 00:06:07,740
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

229
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:09,080
alright, here it comes,

230
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:10,430
he's selling me something,

231
00:06:10,430 --> 00:06:12,070
let me shut that down
right now.

232
00:06:12,270 --> 00:06:13,770
I'm only here because I
made myself

233
00:06:13,770 --> 00:06:15,770
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

234
00:06:15,770 --> 00:06:16,730
that if I ever found

235
00:06:16,730 --> 00:06:17,870
something that helped,

236
00:06:17,870 --> 00:06:18,880
I'd say so.

237
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:21,260
It's called the KenRelief
Red

238
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:22,600
Light Therapy Wrap.

239
00:06:22,890 --> 00:06:24,710
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

240
00:06:24,990 --> 00:06:26,100
It looked like the cheap

241
00:06:26,100 --> 00:06:27,900
knee sleeves off Amazon

242
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:29,380
that did nothing for me.

243
00:06:29,650 --> 00:06:31,620
But I went to their
website anyway,

244
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:32,540
just to see what all

245
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:33,560
the fuss was about.

246
00:06:33,930 --> 00:06:35,970
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

247
00:06:35,970 --> 00:06:38,610
charge $200 a session for,

248
00:06:38,610 --> 00:06:41,470
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

249
00:06:41,470 --> 00:06:42,540
in a wrap you plug

250
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:43,780
into the wall at home.

251
00:06:44,010 --> 00:06:45,630
Two hundred and forty
lights.

252
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:48,370
Red at 660 nanometers

253
00:06:48,370 --> 00:06:51,050
and near-infrared at 850,

254
00:06:51,050 --> 00:06:53,510
run together for the
strongest effect.

255
00:06:53,550 --> 00:06:54,960
Four strength levels.

256
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:57,010
A five to thirty minute
timer.

257
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:58,590
Then I saw the guarantee.

258
00:06:58,680 --> 00:06:59,870
Ninety days.

259
00:06:59,930 --> 00:07:01,820
Results or your money
back,

260
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:04,400
no questions, no store
credit,

261
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:06,290
and you don't even send it
back.

262
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:08,810
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

263
00:07:08,810 --> 00:07:10,520
days to change my mind.

264
00:07:10,570 --> 00:07:12,000
There wasn't much to lose,

265
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,030
so I ordered it.

266
00:07:13,070 --> 00:07:14,350
Two of them, actually.

267
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:16,610
Only the right knee was
replaced,

268
00:07:16,610 --> 00:07:18,750
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

269
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:20,420
and I'd done it for two
years.

270
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:22,580
The left one was carrying
the difference.

271
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:23,230
When it came,

272
00:07:23,230 --> 00:07:25,250
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

273
00:07:25,250 --> 00:07:26,340
because I'd been let down

274
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:28,210
too many times to get
excited.

275
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:30,190
What I felt was warmth.

276
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:32,390
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

277
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:34,360
More like it was coming
from inside

278
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:36,150
the knee and spreading
around it.

279
00:07:36,370 --> 00:07:37,310
And that was it.

280
00:07:37,350 --> 00:07:39,010
That was the whole
experience.

281
00:07:39,050 --> 00:07:40,220
